{"name":"Cosmic Energy","hex":"#9392ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cosmic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or from or pertaining to the cosmos or universe.","Characteristic of the cosmos or universe; inconceivably great; vast."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cosmic"},{"term":"energy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The impetus behind all motion and all activity.","The capacity to do work."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/energy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Energy (esotericism)","blocks":[{"text":"Proponents and practitioners of various esoteric forms of spirituality and alternative medicine refer to a variety of claimed experiences and phenomena as being due to an energy or force that defies measurement or experimentation, and thus are distinct from uses of the term energy in science."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Energy_(esotericism)","wikidata":"Q1970852"},{"title":"Energy","blocks":[{"text":"Energy is the quantitative property that is transferred to a body or to a physical system, recognizable in the capacity to do work and in the form of heat and light. Energy is a conserved quantity – the law of conservation of energy states that the total energy of an isolated system remains constant, although it can be converted in form. The unit of measurement for energy in the International System of Units (SI) is the joule (J)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Plasma_globe_60th.jpg/330px-Plasma_globe_60th.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Energy","wikidata":"Q11379"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Lightning_over_Oradea_Romania_zoom.jpg/500px-Lightning_over_Oradea_Romania_zoom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/